WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:01.610
MAMTHA: Hey.

00:00:01.610 --> 00:00:05.030
Are you looking to both
manage and secure your APIs

00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:06.770
on Google Cloud?

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:09.710
Google offers the
industry-leading API management

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:11.720
platform, Apigee.

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:14.790
And it's really
easy to get started.

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:16.760
My name is [? Mamtha. ?]
And I'm going

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:19.550
to show the setup and
configuration of Apigee API

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:23.093
management on your
Google Cloud project.

00:00:23.093 --> 00:00:24.760
First, let's look at
some prerequisites.

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:27.480
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:30.290
You will need to
create or have access

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:33.740
to a Google Cloud project.

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:35.990
And that project should
have a cloud billing

00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:40.070
account set for it.

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:42.260
Finally, the user
performing the setup

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:45.380
must have the right permissions.

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:47.570
If you have the editor
role on the project,

00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:50.670
that will be more
than sufficient.

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:53.030
Now open the Google
Cloud Console,

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:56.240
select the project in which
you want to configure Apigee.

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:02.180
Then in the search bar,
type Apigee and then

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:05.870
click on the first link.

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:10.430
Alternatively, you can start
from the Apigee pricing page

00:01:10.430 --> 00:01:15.380
and select pay as
you go option there.

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:18.770
Either way, you will be
redirected to the Apigee setup

00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:22.670
page, click on Set Up Apigee.

00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:24.710
This brings you to
the setup wizard.

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:26.340
There are four steps.

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:30.020
First, you need to enable
the APIs for Apigee

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:31.740
and its dependencies.

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:33.920
These are services,
or capabilities,

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:37.220
within Google Cloud that
are required by Apigee.

00:01:37.220 --> 00:01:40.480
Click the Enable API button.

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:42.550
And the wizard will do the work.

00:01:42.550 --> 00:01:45.100
It takes 30 seconds or so.

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:48.470
When you see the blue check
mark, that means it's finished.

00:01:48.470 --> 00:01:49.810
Click Next.

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:53.300
Steps two let you configure
service networking to set

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:56.680
a private connection between
your network, Apigee,

00:01:56.680 --> 00:01:58.810
and Cloud Services.

00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:02.140
If you have a default VPC
network in your project,

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:06.370
the wizard will pre-select as
it is the authorized network.

00:02:06.370 --> 00:02:08.289
These are often
the right choices.

00:02:08.289 --> 00:02:12.160
But you can click the Edit
button to make your own choice.

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:16.630
If you don't yet have a VPC
network, you'll need to pause

00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:18.280
and go and create one.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:20.170
Follow the link shown here.

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:24.385
After you select and confirm the
network and subnet, click Next.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:29.130
The visit configures
the connection

00:02:29.130 --> 00:02:31.890
between the VPC and
the Google services

00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:34.785
to use IP address within
the allowed ranges.

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:40.800
In step three,
hosting an encryption,

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:44.790
here you choose the TCP region
that will host your Apigee

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:48.060
runtime, the gateway
that handle API traffic,

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:52.890
and the GCP region that will
store your analytics data.

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:55.590
They can be different
or the same.

00:02:55.590 --> 00:02:58.890
You can choose any GCP
regions for the runtime.

00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:02.280
But there are more limited set
of choices for the analysis

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:03.360
data.

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:05.280
Along with the
region selection, you

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:09.030
can choose the Google
Cloud managed encryption

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:14.670
or your own encryption for
your runtime instance and data.

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:17.400
Again, in this step,
default configurations

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:18.600
are pre-selected.

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:20.520
Click Edit to modify them.

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:22.710
When you are
satisfied, click Next.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:28.280
In step four, you can
choose whether to allow

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:32.480
inbound requests from internet
to reach Apigee, or allow

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:39.090
only inbound requests if they
originate from within the VPC.

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:42.660
I will choose to allow
external access to API proxies

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:47.170
by selecting Enable
Internet Access.

00:03:47.170 --> 00:03:51.250
We will choose an
automatically-generated domain,

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:53.200
subnet, and SSL certificates.

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:56.325
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:03:58.730 --> 00:04:02.960
After that, click Submit to
begin provisioning process.

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:06.230
In general, the provisioning
process takes up to 40 minutes

00:04:06.230 --> 00:04:07.640
to complete.

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:11.560
Check back later to find my
Apigee organization all set up

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:13.580
with pay-as-you-go billing.

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:14.720
Congratulations.

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:18.200
Your Apigee
organization is ready.

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:20.269
Once this is done,
I can now start

00:04:20.269 --> 00:04:23.720
creating my first
API proxy and explore

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:25.700
the awesomeness of Apigee.

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:28.530
That is the topic
of the next video.

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:31.940
You can start provisioning
your Apigee organization today.

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:34.100
Or if you want to
explore further,

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:38.320
check our further videos and
resources in the link below.

